=begin pod :page-card<Troupes> :nav-order<20>

=TITLE Modules and Frameworks Troupe

=head1 Purpose

To develop the modules and frameworks that make a programming language useful.  

=head1 Activities

L<raku.land|https://raku.land/> has many modules; all we can do here is 
highlight some of the more prominent ones that are frameworks, rather than just 
individual modules.  

=head2 Web-related Frameworks

=item1 The L<hARC stack|https://harcstack.org/>, consisting of:

=item2 L<htmx|https://htmx.org/> for simple dynamic client-side code

=item2		L<Air|https://github.com/librasteve/Air> for coding htmx in Raku

=item2		L<Cro|https://cro.raku.org/> for server-side Raku

=item2		L<Red|https://fco.github.io/Red/>, an ORM, for connecting to 
databases

=item1 L<Elucid8|https://elucid8.org/>, for generating documentation websites 
from Rakudoc

=item1 L<Humming-Bird|https://github.com/rawleyfowler/Humming-Bird>, a simple, 
composable, and performant web-framework, inspired mainly by Sinatra, and 
Express.  

=head1 Terminal UI Frameworks

=item1 L<raku-terminal-ui|https://git.sr.ht/~bduggan/raku-terminal-ui>

=head1 Automation Framework

=item1 L<Sparrow|https://sparrowhub.io/>, a multi-language automation frameworks 
that is useful for

=item2		Configuration Management
=item2		CI/CD
=item2		Testing
=item2		Data Science

=end pod
